WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.829 --> 00:00:09.729
a Web front end server might be in the DMZ,

2
00:00:09.880 --> 00:00:12.319
but it might retrieve data from a database server

3
00:00:12.329 --> 00:00:14.449
that is on the other side of the firewall.

4
00:00:15.529 --> 00:00:16.670
For example,

5
00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.430
you may have a network where you manage your client's personal information,

6
00:00:20.629 --> 00:00:24.559
and even if the data is encrypted or obfuscated by cryptography,

7
00:00:24.690 --> 00:00:26.350
you need to make sure the network is

8
00:00:26.360 --> 00:00:29.110
completely segregated from the rest of the network,

9
00:00:29.120 --> 00:00:33.270
with some secure switches that only an authorised individual has access to.

10
00:00:33.860 --> 00:00:38.119
Only authorised personnel can control the firewall settings and control

11
00:00:38.130 --> 00:00:41.250
the traffic between the Web server and the internal network.

12
00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:42.810
For example,

13
00:00:42.919 --> 00:00:45.009
in a hospital or a doctor's office,

14
00:00:45.020 --> 00:00:48.680
you would have a segregated network for the patient information and billing,

15
00:00:48.779 --> 00:00:51.970
and on the other side would be the electronic medical records.

16
00:00:52.380 --> 00:00:56.470
If they are using a Web based application for medical record services,

17
00:00:56.500 --> 00:01:00.040
they would have a demilitarised zone or segmented areas

18
00:01:00.259 --> 00:01:02.659
and perhaps even behind the firewall.

19
00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:05.199
They have their own specified server to protect

20
00:01:05.209 --> 00:01:07.800
the critical information and keep it segregated.

21
00:01:08.870 --> 00:01:10.849
It is worth noting at this point that

22
00:01:10.860 --> 00:01:13.669
while this course will not explore the specifics,

23
00:01:13.680 --> 00:01:20.050
some networks use a Web application firewall WAF rather than AD MZ network.

24
00:01:20.419 --> 00:01:25.180
The WAF has an internal and an external connection, like a traditional firewall,

25
00:01:25.190 --> 00:01:27.410
with the external traffic being filtered by

26
00:01:27.419 --> 00:01:29.760
the traditional or next generation firewall.

27
00:01:29.769 --> 00:01:30.330
First,

28
00:01:30.709 --> 00:01:33.410
it monitors all traffic encrypted or not

29
00:01:33.419 --> 00:01:35.989
from the outside for malicious behaviour before

30
00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:39.690
passing commands to a Web server that may be internal to the network.